{"title":"2019 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, both centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, have radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, whose interior lies in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> but in the exterior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, has vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, and the line containing side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />. Segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51eee107f2b552caca08ea4f3cd1078a32b22ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AO}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea6d895bbea72f6c2affb547c4b49731f6f09d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{BP}{CP} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"39\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/1/fd1b574f8baf6ba4524bd9e9715f7f60eed62211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{m}{\\sqrt{n}} - \\dfrac{p}{\\sqrt{q}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"78\" height=\"39\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41dd88ffd5a00b4c32a030d6ebb2e25bd076d456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}(m,n) = \\text{gcd}(p,q) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740b7804fdc9546a926406b6b1e2b10490f85a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8baa288cc33e3c4093b5c696b57db8a5a9d18a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phantom{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e2672158d4244028c2b3b7a35575a6703f273e7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 42 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }86 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 92 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 114 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 130$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"416\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/8374efc0c580bf65c2bd3438f17939e93bfd601a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(20cm); draw(circle((0,0), 20)); label(&quot;$\\omega$&quot;, (0,0), 4.05*20*dir(149)*20/21); draw(circle((0,0), 17)); label(&quot;$\\gamma$&quot;, (0,0), 4.05*17*dir(149)*20/21); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, (0,0), E); pair aa = (-20, 0); dot(aa); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, aa, W); draw((-20,0)--(0,0)); real a = (-20 + (80/sqrt(13) - 34/sqrt(3))*(sqrt(13)/sqrt(12))*(sqrt(3)/2)); real ans = (80/sqrt(13) - 34/sqrt(3)); dot((a,0)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, (a, 0), dir(290)*0.58); pair s = ((12*a + 0)/13, 0-sqrt(12)*a/13); dot(s); label(&quot;$S$&quot;, s, dir(135)); pair c = (a + 1/4*ans*1/sqrt(13), 0 + 1/4*ans*sqrt(12)/sqrt(13)); dot(c); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, c, dir(110)); pair m = (a - 1/4*ans*1/sqrt(13), 0 - 1/4*ans*sqrt(12)/sqrt(13)); dot(m); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, m, dir(285)); pair b = (a - 3/4*ans*1/sqrt(13), 0 - 3/4*ans*sqrt(12)/sqrt(13)); dot(b); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, b, S); draw(b--s); draw(s--(0,0)); draw(aa--b); draw(aa--c); draw(aa--m); markscalefactor=0.1; draw(rightanglemark(s,m,aa,3.4)); draw(rightanglemark((0,0),s,m,3.4)); [/asy]\" width=\"945\" height=\"925\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of tangency between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f4d402805185ed8801a24712f8b2a2c0c508ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM \\perp BS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec5e275057b37f63334b19c85045a32122b7c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OS \\perp BS$\" width=\"77\" height=\"12\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b268142ac98f21461bfc9a1e691651bd2da36a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OAM \\cong \\angle AOS$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294347a3de9a7ba97d50c7b610955e7095b31e02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AMP \\cong \\angle OSP$\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb0720d99fe0a566012e99f18d2fd84bc50c8cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PMA \\sim \\triangle PSO$\" width=\"144\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, then it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc168c1d0589e9c6b9dcbe784244e8170d5bf677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05ed26c236384064b8db6c2593c541c1c4c1e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PM = \\frac{s}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"33\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396b67c512d3c1bfdb46115f4dd48cba84063bac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{4}s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94a923451a074ad7376351b1fdd0cce095d9ded.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AM}{AP} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"101\" height=\"48\" />. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2e254d880bbe2e5e53ad7655bf03a1af3e37dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AM + SO}{AO} = \\frac{AM}{AP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"38\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb0720d99fe0a566012e99f18d2fd84bc50c8cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PMA \\sim \\triangle PSO$\" width=\"144\" height=\"13\" />) so this gives us the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f0577c95257dbfec03c9739060758943698cd3a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}s + 17}{20} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"48\" />\nto solve for the side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d5951625083116db014037931a6e4186fb924568.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{2}s + 17\\sqrt{13} = 40\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad3fd3076309d82e5cd8be1b043b4b772292ca6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{2}s = 40\\sqrt{3} - 17\\sqrt{13}\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacde4156a3a29777f52fc27aa0c822aa79c4b99.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = \\frac{80}{\\sqrt{13}} - \\frac{34}{\\sqrt{3}} = AB\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"42\" />\nThe problem asks for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a2cf3b4d9d0de2a48fdda28cef0c44201d3955b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n + p + q = 80 + 13 + 34 + 3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 130}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"363\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the diagram above. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of tangency between line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6df1ef11bffe0ecf35b0082a7e1e3ec11f38baf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = 3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89ff22040a0ce519ee2a988391c2be12dd147451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the side length of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, which is the value we need to find. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e8a50b34c26310c6c8a223efe45df5b571ed90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABP = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, we can apply the Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a781c1980ff6e4c2f2ae64ead9e4dd3e87dbb1bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/3247a16a4f54c330916cda9179ea241c7c012849.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AP = \\sqrt{(3x)^2 + (4x)^2 - 2(3x)(4x)\\cos(60^\\circ)} = \\sqrt{13}x\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Next, we use the Law of Cosines to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/8466eeaa4c9cc111db381822e8e72f8230677752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle APB)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c90052dc70c344b0d05e36ce32978406e6e16a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\angle APB) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dcab16d6a09e45436f7b9476391c37515455ee2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5ad0c1f02124854d4c7aad2cf1e63c225024638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OPS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> are vertical angles, they are equal. Therefore:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1649180fbcf791e1df957acd2c2ba37675d1fa04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\angle OPS) = \\cos(\\angle APB) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Using the Pythagorean identity, we find the sine of the angle:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319af2e6bc42746fac8082fee4392de9aabdd728.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\angle OPS) = \\frac{\\sqrt{12}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>We are given that the radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6694bd877a003b6f0f98c057f03590701ab5de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OS = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, and the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1528c9f15cb77f35a16414140f6a4b8f615089c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP = 20 - \\sqrt{13}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" />. Using the right triangle properties, we can set up the ratio:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c22eeffabd1824c82ca2845d477c210ed34a126c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\angle OPS) = \\frac{\\sqrt{12}}{\\sqrt{13}} = \\frac{OS}{OP} = \\frac{17}{20 - \\sqrt{13}x}\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Solving this equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/491959baf8eb58ae76fad78a4414ebbc2e003b35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{13}} - \\frac{17}{2\\sqrt{12}}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to find the total side length:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/2097d660fdaef65e100c3001149ca571aaf23338.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x = \\frac{80}{\\sqrt{13}} - \\frac{34}{\\sqrt{3}}\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>We want to find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b1317658aa8bae1cb9152ef19e0ffad3500359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n + p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />, which gives the final answer:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb8fe21137269c51322445caa0df83a1961029d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 130}\\]\" width=\"72\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~ hb12\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2eASfdhEyUE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2eASfdhEyUE</a>\n</p><p>Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk -\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CaYgfNEUBwA&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvLgfgbaTLDaV_jRYfn1A-x_&amp;index=2\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CaYgfNEUBwA&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvLgfgbaTLDaV_jRYfn1A-x_&amp;index=2</a>\n- AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A\" title=\"2019 AMC 12A\">2019 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/ind